{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T16:12:27.845Z","data":{"text":"Done. Both the task verify and the proposal verify (`pnpm verify`, exit 0) pass.\n\n## Summary\n\n**Added `src/cli/remote-plan.ts`** (148 lines) — the client side of cli-foundation \"Planning against a server\":\n- `remoteWorkRoot(server, home?)` builds `<home>/.osq/remote/<host>/<project>` with `:` → `-` in the host.\n- `planOnServer` streams output unchanged under `--print`; otherwise collects stdout and, on a successful handoff line, downloads `api/files/<folder>`, replaces the working copy with exactly the downloaded files, and rewrites only the handoff line's path. Every other line prints unchanged.\n- `lintOnServer` finds each id's working copy with `matchesFolder`, uploads every file except `.run/` through the PUT endpoint (failing on a refused upload before linting), then forwards `lint`.\n- Both throw a nonzero last line as a `CommandError` with its message/exit code/next step, using `runOnServer`, `readFromServer`, and `writeToServer`.\n\n**Added `tests/remote-plan.test.ts`** — all four \"Planning against a server\" scenarios against a real port-0 server with a site, `createForwardedRunner(root, { home })`, a temp project (default config, `vcs` off), a temp home, and string writers. The lint test compares against in-process `lintCommand`.\n\nVerified constraints: no exported name ends in `Command`, no `exit` identifier, no direct process writes; source file under 250 lines and functions under 80; no `skipped` in `src/`; all existing tests unchanged. Result written to `openspec/changes/162-remote-cli/.run/results/3.md`."}}
