{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-09T23:09:30.706Z","data":{"text":"Task complete.\n\n## Summary\n\nAdded the client side of plan-download / lint-upload:\n\n- **`src/cli/remote-plan.ts`** (188 lines) — exports `remoteWorkRoot`, `planOnServer`, `lintOnServer`.\n  - `remoteWorkRoot` builds `<home>/.osq/remote/<host>/<project>` with `:` → `-`.\n  - `planOnServer` forwards via `runOnServer`, passes `--print` through, otherwise collects stdout, matches the handoff line, downloads with `readFromServer('api/files/<folder>')`, replaces the working copy with exactly the downloaded files and rewrites the line's path.\n  - `lintOnServer` resolves each id with `matchesFolder`, reads the working copy except `.run/` as `/`-separated paths, uploads with `writeToServer(..., 'PUT', ...)`, then forwards `lint`.\n  - Both throw a `CommandError` with the last line's message, exit code and next step.\n- **`tests/remote-plan.test.ts`** — the four \"Planning against a server\" scenarios against a real `startWebServer` on port 0 with `createForwardedRunner(root, { home })`, plus `--print` and no-ids cases. The lint scenario compares forwarded output with an in-process `lintCommand(['001'], { cwd: root, ... })` after the upload.\n\nTagged each export with `@scenario cli-foundation`/`@adr 014`. No exported `*Command`, no `exit` identifiers, no direct process writes, 188 ≤ 250 lines.\n\n**Verification:** task verify green; `pnpm verify` green; full CLI suite 3677/3677 pass. Result written to `openspec/changes/162-remote-cli/.run/results/3.md`.\n\nOne deviation noted in the result: the fixture adds a lintable `proposal.md`/`tasks/1.md`, a passing `verify.cjs`, and `tests/helpers.ts`'s fake OpenSpec validator so the upload scenario exercises a successful lint, beyond the `brief.md` + `.run/manifest.json` the task named."}}
